//
// Normative rule hstatus_vtw_op (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   When VTW=1 (and assuming mstatus.TW=0), an attempt in VS-mode to execute WFI raises a virtual-
//     instruction exception if the WFI does not complete within an implementation-specific, bounded
//     time limit.
//
// Context:
//   A WFI may complete (no trap) or, with VTW=1, raise virtual-instruction after a bounded time, so
//     both are legal with VTW=1; illegal-instruction is not. With VTW=0 and TW=0, VS-mode WFI may
//     wait for an interrupt, so those cases provide a wake-up source: a VS-level software interrupt
//     delegated to VS-mode (hideleg[2]=1, hvip.VSSIP=1), enabled in vsie and globally disabled
//     (vsstatus.SIE=0), which makes WFI complete without being taken. HS-mode uses sip.SSIP the
//     same way.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. VTW=1, no interrupt pending: VS-mode WFI completes or raises virtual-instruction (xtval 0 or
//     0x10500073, from VS).
//   2. VTW=1 with the wake-up source: completes or raises virtual-instruction.
//   3. VTW=0 with the wake-up source: WFI completes without a trap.
//   4. VTW=1 does not affect HS-mode: with an HS wake-up source, HS-mode WFI completes without a
//     trap.
//   5. VTW back to 0: VS-mode WFI with the wake-up source completes again.
//
